#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186714460 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-12x-2y=8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186714447} {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6x+8y=-24" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186714453} {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9x+12y=-24" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186714455} {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9x+12y=-36" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186714463} {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-18x-3y=-6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186714464}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-12x-2y=8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186714447} :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186714456}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "aefd6738-17b4-5ae3-9465-79de326525f7" :question/problem "Which of the following is a distinct line parallel to $-12x-2y=-4$?" :question/worked-solution "For two distinct nonvertical lines to be parallel, they must have the same slope.\n\nTo find the slope of $-12x-2y=-4$, convert to slope-intercept form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n-12x-2y &= -4 \\\\\n-2y &= 12x-4 \\\\\ny &= -6x+2\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe slope is the coefficient of $x$, so the required slope is $-6$.\n\nRewrite the choices in slope-intercept form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n-12x-2y=8 &\\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad y=-6x-4 \\\\\n9x+12y=-24 &\\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad y=-\\frac{3}{4}x-2 \\\\\n-18x-3y=-6 &\\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad y=-6x+2 \\\\\n9x+12y=-36 &\\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad y=-\\frac{3}{4}x-3 \\\\\n-6x+8y=-24 &\\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad y=\\frac{3}{4}x-3\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe line $-18x-3y=-6$ has both the same slope $-6$ and the same $y$-intercept $2$ as the given line. It is the same line, so it is not a distinct parallel line.\n\nThe line $-12x-2y=8$ has slope $-6$ and $y$-intercept $-4$, different from $2$. Therefore, it is a distinct parallel line.\n\n$$\n-12x-2y=8\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186714467 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6x+8y=-24" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186714457} {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9x+12y=-24" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186714465} {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-18x-3y=-6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186714468} {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9x+12y=-36" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186714469} {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-12x-2y=8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186714470}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-18x-3y=-6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186714468} :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186714446}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "d64f7da5-9842-5d17-8bd6-ebac5d6d13c1" :question/problem "Which of the following is a distinct line parallel to $-12x-2y=8$?" :question/worked-solution "For two distinct nonvertical lines to be parallel, they must have the same slope.\n\nTo find the slope of $-12x-2y=8$, convert to slope-intercept form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n-12x-2y &= 8 \\\\\n-2y &= 12x+8 \\\\\ny &= -6x-4\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe slope is the coefficient of $x$, so the required slope is $-6$.\n\nRewrite the choices in slope-intercept form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n-12x-2y=8 &\\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad y=-6x-4 \\\\\n9x+12y=-24 &\\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad y=-\\frac{3}{4}x-2 \\\\\n-18x-3y=-6 &\\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad y=-6x+2 \\\\\n9x+12y=-36 &\\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad y=-\\frac{3}{4}x-3 \\\\\n-6x+8y=-24 &\\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad y=\\frac{3}{4}x-3\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe line $-12x-2y=8$ has both the same slope $-6$ and the same $y$-intercept $-4$ as the given line. It is the same line, so it is not a distinct parallel line.\n\nThe line $-18x-3y=-6$ has slope $-6$ and $y$-intercept $2$, different from $-4$. Therefore, it is a distinct parallel line.\n\n$$\n-18x-3y=-6\n$$"}]}
